<title>JAPAN: Japan end-Oct coffee stocks fall 18.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan end-Oct coffee stocks fall 18.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's warehouse stocks of coffee at the end of October totalled 64,833 tonnes, down 18.8 percent from a year earlier, the Agriculture Ministry said.</p>
<p>At the end of October last year, stocks in Japan, the world's third-biggest coffee consumer after the United States and Germany, totalled 79,857 tonnes, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Details of the coffee stocks are as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Oct 96	  Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p> Brazil	     10,049	   9,393	18,064</p>
<p> Colombia	   15,093	  15,507	15,697</p>
<p> Indonesia	  10,929	  10,196	11,572</p>
<p> Central America  15,070	  16,091	18,578</p>
<p> Others	     13,692	  14,164	15,946</p>
<p> Total		64,833	  65,351	79,857</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
